WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.066
A new agent session should not mean explaining the same project

00:00:04.066 --> 00:00:07.932
instruction again. Here is one lesson from our Harbour project brief.

00:00:09.332 --> 00:00:14.654
I save the validation instruction as memory, with a tag identifying its source. The

00:00:14.654 --> 00:00:19.977
saved item contains the exact lesson, not just a label saying something was captured.

00:00:21.377 --> 00:00:25.733
That command has finished. A new process opens the saved item by

00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:30.453
its identifier. The same instruction is still there, ready to inspect or export.

00:00:31.853 --> 00:00:36.489
The project role has a small knowledge graph. Validate brief, brief validation, and

00:00:36.489 --> 00:00:41.481
the check option name the same concept. The note also names the project brief.

00:00:42.881 --> 00:00:47.369
I search for validate brief. The graph retrieves the saved instruction and its

00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:52.202
source tag. This is the actual stored text, rather than a newly generated answer.

00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:58.337
An unrelated question returns no memory. So does the finance role, and

00:00:58.337 --> 00:01:03.072
a separate empty store. Roles shape retrieval; separate folders hold separate stores.

00:01:04.472 --> 00:01:08.071
Download the public brief, graph, commands and saved results. Next,

00:01:08.071 --> 00:01:11.669
we will use the same project to show a failed

00:01:11.669 --> 00:01:15.268
command, a reviewed correction, and what an agent actually executes.
